1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:00,935
Friday,

2
00:00:00,935 --> 00:00:01,743
five o'clock.

3
00:00:01,743 --> 00:00:04,104
Someone pushes a small change to main,

4
00:00:04,104 --> 00:00:06,217
and the whole team's build breaks.

5
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:08,906
A team release workflow stops that.

6
00:00:08,906 --> 00:00:11,534
Automated checks run before code is shared,

7
00:00:11,534 --> 00:00:13,978
and every release gets a version number.

8
00:00:14,528 --> 00:00:16,891
Today you build one: a check script,

9
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:18,859
a gate that blocks bad pushes,

10
00:00:18,859 --> 00:00:20,106
a CI workflow file,

11
00:00:20,106 --> 00:00:21,419
and tagged releases.

12
00:00:21,969 --> 00:00:24,785
As always, there is a lab with a checker at the end.

13
00:00:26,835 --> 00:00:32,403
A release workflow is a path that every change walks. Branch, check, review, merge, tag.

14
00:00:32,953 --> 00:00:37,911
A check is a small script that answers one question: is this change safe?

15
00:00:37,911 --> 00:00:39,744
It exits with zero for yes,

16
00:00:39,744 --> 00:00:41,102
and non-zero for no.

17
00:00:41,652 --> 00:00:43,896
Run checks on your own computer first,

18
00:00:43,896 --> 00:00:45,786
so you find mistakes in seconds.

19
00:00:45,786 --> 00:00:48,266
A pre push gate can even run them for you.

20
00:00:48,816 --> 00:00:50,712
Run them again on the server,

21
00:00:50,712 --> 00:00:51,105
in CI,

22
00:00:51,105 --> 00:00:52,544
on every pull request,

23
00:00:52,544 --> 00:00:54,768
so nothing unchecked reaches main.

24
00:00:55,318 --> 00:00:56,562
When main is ready,

25
00:00:56,562 --> 00:01:00,228
tag it with a version number: major dot minor dot patch.

26
00:01:00,228 --> 00:01:02,912
A tag is a permanent label on one commit.

27
00:01:03,462 --> 00:01:05,830
That is the whole workflow. Let us build it.

28
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:13,576
Let us see it live. A tiny shop script, and the team check. Go in. Type: CD, shop.

29
00:01:14,126 --> 00:01:17,603
Here is the team check. Type: cat, check dot S H.

30
00:01:18,153 --> 00:01:20,933
Three checks: the syntax of every script,

31
00:01:20,933 --> 00:01:22,696
no leftover to do markers,

32
00:01:22,696 --> 00:01:23,645
and the tests.

33
00:01:23,645 --> 00:01:24,119
Run it.

34
00:01:24,119 --> 00:01:26,153
Type: dot slash check dot S H.

35
00:01:26,703 --> 00:01:28,216
Now break something.

36
00:01:28,216 --> 00:01:29,577
Add a broken line.

37
00:01:29,577 --> 00:01:30,409
Type: echo,

38
00:01:30,409 --> 00:01:30,862
quote,

39
00:01:30,862 --> 00:01:31,240
oops,

40
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:32,072
open paren,

41
00:01:32,072 --> 00:01:32,526
quote,

42
00:01:32,526 --> 00:01:33,358
two arrows,

43
00:01:33,358 --> 00:01:34,341
shop dot S H.

44
00:01:34,891 --> 00:01:38,667
Run the check again. Type: dot slash check dot S H.

45
00:01:39,217 --> 00:01:39,888
It failed,

46
00:01:39,888 --> 00:01:41,366
and it names the file.

47
00:01:41,366 --> 00:01:43,851
A check speaks through its exit code.

48
00:01:43,851 --> 00:01:44,321
See it.

49
00:01:44,321 --> 00:01:45,060
Type: echo,

50
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:45,530
dollar,

51
00:01:45,530 --> 00:01:46,470
question mark.

52
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:48,371
One means failure.

53
00:01:48,371 --> 00:01:49,798
Zero means success.

54
00:01:49,798 --> 00:01:52,650
Undo the mistake with a tool you know.

55
00:01:52,650 --> 00:01:54,001
Type: git restore,

56
00:01:54,001 --> 00:01:54,977
shop dot S H.

57
00:01:55,527 --> 00:01:59,410
Run the check once more. Type: dot slash check dot S H.

58
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:04,013
Checks passed. The same answer, every time, for everyone on the team.

59
00:02:06,063 --> 00:02:08,836
Now the gate. Go in. Type: CD, shop.

60
00:02:09,386 --> 00:02:13,236
A git hook is a script that Git runs at a moment you choose.

61
00:02:13,236 --> 00:02:15,289
This one runs before every push.

62
00:02:15,289 --> 00:02:15,930
Type: cat,

63
00:02:15,930 --> 00:02:16,829
dot git hooks,

64
00:02:16,829 --> 00:02:17,213
slash,

65
00:02:17,213 --> 00:02:18,112
pre dash push.

66
00:02:18,662 --> 00:02:19,844
It runs the check,

67
00:02:19,844 --> 00:02:22,406
and blocks the push if the check fails.

68
00:02:22,406 --> 00:02:24,442
Turn it on for this repository.

69
00:02:24,442 --> 00:02:25,559
Type: git config,

70
00:02:25,559 --> 00:02:26,873
core dot hooks path,

71
00:02:26,873 --> 00:02:27,792
dot git hooks.

72
00:02:28,342 --> 00:02:30,048
Now make a bad change.

73
00:02:30,048 --> 00:02:30,902
Type: echo,

74
00:02:30,902 --> 00:02:31,367
quote,

75
00:02:31,367 --> 00:02:31,755
oops,

76
00:02:31,755 --> 00:02:32,608
open paren,

77
00:02:32,608 --> 00:02:33,073
quote,

78
00:02:33,073 --> 00:02:33,926
two arrows,

79
00:02:33,926 --> 00:02:34,934
shop dot S H.

80
00:02:35,484 --> 00:02:39,410
Commit it. Type: git commit, dash A M, quote, Quick change, quote.

81
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:43,693
Try to push it to the team. Type: git push, origin main.

82
00:02:44,243 --> 00:02:44,785
Blocked.

83
00:02:44,785 --> 00:02:47,493
The bad commit never left your computer.

84
00:02:47,493 --> 00:02:48,441
It is private,

85
00:02:48,441 --> 00:02:50,067
so a reset is safe here.

86
00:02:50,067 --> 00:02:51,150
Type: git reset,

87
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:52,166
dash dash hard,

88
00:02:52,166 --> 00:02:53,182
head tilde one.

89
00:02:53,732 --> 00:02:59,236
Now a good change. Type: echo, quote, Free shipping, quote, two arrows, notes dot text.

90
00:02:59,786 --> 00:03:02,580
Stage it. Type: git add, notes dot text.

91
00:03:03,130 --> 00:03:07,162
Commit it. Type: git commit, dash M, quote, Add shipping note, quote.

92
00:03:07,712 --> 00:03:10,635
Push again. Type: git push, origin main.

93
00:03:11,185 --> 00:03:15,558
The check ran, passed, and the push went through. Bad changes stop at your door.

94
00:03:17,608 --> 00:03:21,171
Same check, on the server. Go in. Type: CD, shop.

95
00:03:21,721 --> 00:03:24,960
This file lives in the repository.

96
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:25,913
Type: cat,

97
00:03:25,913 --> 00:03:30,297
dot github slash workflows slash CI dot yamel.

98
00:03:30,847 --> 00:03:36,393
On: pull request. This workflow starts on every pull request, and on every push to main.

99
00:03:36,943 --> 00:03:38,483
Runs on: ubuntu latest.

100
00:03:38,483 --> 00:03:41,832
Git hub gives it a fresh Ubuntu machine each time,

101
00:03:41,832 --> 00:03:44,175
so it never depends on your laptop.

102
00:03:44,725 --> 00:03:49,504
Uses: actions slash checkout. This step downloads your code onto that machine.

103
00:03:50,054 --> 00:03:55,601
Run: dot slash check dot S H. The same script as your gate. One check, two places.

104
00:03:56,151 --> 00:03:56,477
Then,

105
00:03:56,477 --> 00:03:58,240
in the repository settings,

106
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:01,438
turn on branch protection and require this check.

107
00:04:01,438 --> 00:04:02,679
Red means no merge.

108
00:04:03,229 --> 00:04:05,738
This screen is a labelled illustration.

109
00:04:05,738 --> 00:04:07,283
Git hub runs it for you,

110
00:04:07,283 --> 00:04:11,015
and the workflow file is the real one from the repository.

111
00:04:13,065 --> 00:04:15,988
Now releases. Go in. Type: CD, shop.

112
00:04:16,538 --> 00:04:21,956
A release is a tag: a permanent name on one commit. List the tags. Type: git tag.

113
00:04:22,506 --> 00:04:23,707
One tag so far,

114
00:04:23,707 --> 00:04:25,628
V one dot zero dot zero.

115
00:04:25,628 --> 00:04:27,549
What changed since then?

116
00:04:27,549 --> 00:04:28,669
Type: git log,

117
00:04:28,669 --> 00:04:30,190
dash dash one line,

118
00:04:30,190 --> 00:04:32,111
V one dot zero dot zero,

119
00:04:32,111 --> 00:04:32,751
dot dot,

120
00:04:32,751 --> 00:04:33,152
head.

121
00:04:33,702 --> 00:04:36,686
Those two lines are your release notes.

122
00:04:36,686 --> 00:04:39,441
Git can also tell you where you are.

123
00:04:39,441 --> 00:04:40,895
Type: git describe,

124
00:04:40,895 --> 00:04:42,043
dash dash tags.

125
00:04:42,593 --> 00:04:45,768
Two commits after V one dot zero dot zero.

126
00:04:45,768 --> 00:04:48,263
A new feature earns a minor bump.

127
00:04:48,263 --> 00:04:51,060
Make an annotated tag with a message.

128
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:52,118
Type: git tag,

129
00:04:52,118 --> 00:04:52,647
dash A,

130
00:04:52,647 --> 00:04:54,386
V one dot one dot zero,

131
00:04:54,386 --> 00:04:54,915
dash M,

132
00:04:54,915 --> 00:04:55,369
quote,

133
00:04:55,369 --> 00:04:56,881
Add discount option,

134
00:04:56,881 --> 00:04:57,334
quote.

135
00:04:57,884 --> 00:05:00,410
Tags do not travel by themselves.

136
00:05:00,410 --> 00:05:01,481
Push this one.

137
00:05:01,481 --> 00:05:02,629
Type: git push,

138
00:05:02,629 --> 00:05:03,164
origin,

139
00:05:03,164 --> 00:05:04,924
V one dot one dot zero.

140
00:05:05,474 --> 00:05:10,637
Check what the team can see. Type: git L S remote, dash dash tags, origin.

141
00:05:11,187 --> 00:05:12,821
Both releases are there.

142
00:05:12,821 --> 00:05:14,659
Major for breaking changes,

143
00:05:14,659 --> 00:05:15,952
minor for features,

144
00:05:15,952 --> 00:05:17,042
patch for fixes.

145
00:05:17,042 --> 00:05:18,335
Use annotated tags,

146
00:05:18,335 --> 00:05:20,445
so every release has an author,

147
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:20,922
a date,

148
00:05:20,922 --> 00:05:21,875
and a message.

149
00:05:24,025 --> 00:05:26,798
Your task, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

150
00:05:27,348 --> 00:05:29,863
The lab is lab sixty-five dot S H,

151
00:05:29,863 --> 00:05:33,635
in the academy slash lab folder of git hub dot com,

152
00:05:33,635 --> 00:05:35,115
slash it dash waves,

153
00:05:35,115 --> 00:05:36,816
slash dev ops dash A I.

154
00:05:36,816 --> 00:05:38,517
Install it like before,

155
00:05:38,517 --> 00:05:39,700
then run lab up.

156
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:43,118
It builds a shop repository and a shared copy.

157
00:05:43,118 --> 00:05:45,487
The last commit broke the shop script,

158
00:05:45,487 --> 00:05:46,672
so the checks fail.

159
00:05:47,222 --> 00:05:51,040
One: run the check, read the failure, and fix the bug in a new commit.

160
00:05:51,590 --> 00:05:55,196
Two: turn on the gate, with git config core dot hooks path.

161
00:05:55,746 --> 00:05:59,052
Three: push main to origin. The gate must let it through.

162
00:05:59,602 --> 00:06:04,914
Four: create an annotated tag, V one dot zero dot zero, and push the tag.

163
00:06:05,464 --> 00:06:07,205
Five: in answers dot text,

164
00:06:07,205 --> 00:06:11,756
write which part of the version you raise for a bug fix only: major,

165
00:06:11,756 --> 00:06:12,158
minor,

166
00:06:12,158 --> 00:06:12,760
or patch.

167
00:06:13,310 --> 00:06:17,150
Then run lab check. Five pass lines. Check, gate, tag.

168
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:21,184
Six points, and you need all six.

169
00:06:21,734 --> 00:06:23,611
The checker shows five pass lines.

170
00:06:24,161 --> 00:06:26,892
You fixed the bug in a new commit, and the checks pass.

171
00:06:27,442 --> 00:06:29,725
The gate is on, and your push went through it.

172
00:06:30,275 --> 00:06:33,069
Your tag is annotated, and it is on origin.

173
00:06:33,619 --> 00:06:35,987
You can explain major, minor, and patch.

174
00:06:36,537 --> 00:06:38,180
You ran lab down to clean up.

175
00:06:38,730 --> 00:06:40,351
To pass, you need all six.

176
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:45,238
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

177
00:06:45,788 --> 00:06:48,007
One: install the lab, and run lab up.

178
00:06:48,557 --> 00:06:50,605
Two: run the check, and fix the bug.

179
00:06:51,155 --> 00:06:52,563
Three: turn on the gate.

180
00:06:53,113 --> 00:06:54,926
Four: push main to origin.

181
00:06:55,476 --> 00:06:58,058
Five: tag V one dot zero dot zero,

182
00:06:58,058 --> 00:06:59,045
push the tag,

183
00:06:59,045 --> 00:07:01,095
and write answers dot text.

184
00:07:01,095 --> 00:07:02,538
Then run lab check.

185
00:07:03,088 --> 00:07:04,560
Six: run lab down.

186
00:07:05,110 --> 00:07:06,944
Pause the video, and begin now.

187
00:07:22,494 --> 00:07:23,369
Quick check.

188
00:07:23,919 --> 00:07:25,881
What does a check's exit code tell you?

189
00:07:26,431 --> 00:07:29,290
Why run checks both on your computer and in CI?

190
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,419
What does a pre push gate do?

191
00:07:31,969 --> 00:07:35,062
What do major, minor, and patch mean in a version number?

192
00:07:35,612 --> 00:07:38,086
Objective covered: M C zero seven,

193
00:07:38,086 --> 00:07:39,177
objective nine,

194
00:07:39,177 --> 00:07:42,524
a team release workflow with automated checks.

195
00:07:43,074 --> 00:07:45,143
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

196
00:07:55,693 --> 00:07:59,683
Next: the mastery lesson for the whole Git and Git hub masterclass.

197
00:08:00,233 --> 00:08:03,561
